      "id": 1,
      "text": "Bannister takes its name from Asahel Bannister, who settled there in 1881 after leaving Jackson.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://99wfmk.com/bannister-michigan-gratiot-county/",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "A post office opened in 1883, and the Ann Arbor Railroad opened a depot in 1884, sparking early growth.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://99wfmk.com/bannister-michigan-gratiot-county/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Maple River ran through Bannister, yet locals dubbed it the “Gurgling Maple” because it made no noise.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://99wfmk.com/bannister-michigan-gratiot-county/",
